ds) to control later.  \n- If the landlord only has a high single (like the other 2 or an Ace), they can beat my 2 but then I still have 3 low cards and teammate can potentially take over.  \n- If I play a low card instead (♦5), the landlord could play a medium card and possibly finish next turn without using a bomb, making it harder for my teammate to intervene.  \n\nThe biggest risk is if the landlord holds a rocket (two jokers) — but rocket beats anything anyway, so playing the 2 doesn’t change that. If they have a bomb, better to force it now while my teammate has many cards to respond.  \n\nTherefore, the best move is to play **♣2** to pressure the landlord and leave myself with 3 low cards that my teammate can potentially cover after the landlord’s response.  \n\n**Answer:**  \n{"cards": ["♣2"]}'}
